PETSELFTEST1
# V9 bookshelf: Story opens the shelf first, the dial picks, press opens.
# Card: TWO OR MORE books in /books (forest_friends.kpb plus reader_test.kpb
#   from: python -m tools.make_reader_test_book --output build/reader-test).
# No "book" step on purpose: that step keeps the direct open (v4_book_reader).
# 1 Story press: shelf (full), dial moves the ring (partials), press opens
#   the picked book; hold = home. 2 Story again: the shelf comes back on the
#   book read last; hold on the shelf = home. Counted from "mark begin".
# expect min:PET_SHELF_OPEN 2
# expect min:PET_SHELF_VIEW 5
# expect min:PET_SHELF_PICK 1
# expect min:ok=1 1
# expect none:ok=0 0
# expect min:PET_BOOK_OPEN 1
# expect min:PET_BOOK_HOME 1
# expect min:PET_SHELF_HOME 1
# expect none:PET_BOOK_DRAW_FAILED 0
# expect none:PET_BOOK_MISSING 0
# expect none:PET_SHELF_NO_MEMORY 0
# expect none:PET_SELFTEST_ABORT 0
# expect commits 4
# expect selftest_done 1
# expect max_partial_ms 3000
# expect max_full_ms 12000
phase day
volume 15
waitidle 60000
pet
wait 7000
# Normalize to home: press opens the preselected Story, hold returns home.
tap press 9000
hold press 1500 7000
mark begin
# Story: the shelf (full refresh), ring on the first book.
tap press 9000
# Ring moves: next, next, back (partials; the row may flip on a big card).
tap down 2500
tap down 2500
tap up 2500
# Press opens the picked book (page 1, full refresh), then hold goes home.
tap press 14000
hold press 1500 7000
# Story again: the shelf, ring on the book read last; hold = home.
tap press 9000
tap down 2500
hold press 1500 7000
pet
wait 5000
end
